  Fort Ludious?

  Spell of detect treasure only shows you the top item on a 
square.  So you can only be sure that the Bell isn't on an
empty square.  Any square with an item on it (water, lava, land,
etc.) will have to be manually checked.

  Check all the water squares with any items on them.  I think 
the invocation items pop to the surface when they're in a water 
square that gets frozen.  Double check that, then start freezing 
water if it does work.  (Spell of cone of cold looks good here.)


  When checking items on the floor:

    - Don't levitate.
    - Turn on autopickup.
      - If you have autopickup exceptions, put "<*bell*" in your 
        autopickup exceptions.  Double check the pattern by 
        having autopickup automatically pick up a bell (any 
        bell). (You'll have to re-add the pattern every time you 
        save and restore the game re-start.)

      - If you don't have autopickup exceptions, make sure tools 
        are in your auto-pickup item types to be picked up.  
        Double check this by having autopickup automatically pick
        up a tool. (This will save a *lot* of manual checking of 
        lists of items on the ground.)


  I don't know if other monsters can pick up the invocation items
or not.  Just remember that what the spell of detect treasure 
showed the last time it was cast may not reflect the current 
location of items on a level.


  I'd probably actually get autopickup configured to do the hard 
part, then go to every level and move every non-buried, 
non-frozen item on it onto one big pile on the level.

  Remember, the only thing you can trust with detect treasure is
that the Bell of Opening can't be on an empty square.  Even 
frozen water squares with an item on them will need to be 
manually checked.


  Start with your stash level(s).  If you get autopickup properly
configured and re-cast detect treasure it should be relatively 
simple.  Then the bottom level of the Quest and work up.

  After the Quest levels, Fort Ludios, the Castle, and any other
water squares.

  Don't forget to move everything to a pile on one square so
re-checking a level with Detect Treasure and autopickup is 
simple.


  Someone else had this problem once.  Google for what they did.
(It's not in the above ideas.)


